# Addon module map

## Non-negotiables

- Prefer extending planned modules over new top-level files
- Expand TOC only when the file exists
- UI→Core→Data / Net→Core→Data; never Core→UI
- Lifecycle detail: `toc-lifecycle.mdc`. Style: `lua-cob-modules.mdc`

## Put code here

| `COB` key | File | Owns |
|-----------|------|------|
| `Ranks` | `Data/Ranks.lua` | ids, titles |
| `DB` | `Core/DB.lua` | `ChurchOfBeefDB` shape, defaults, migrate |
| `Common` | `Core/Common.lua` | identity keys, injectable clock |
| `Officer` | `Core/Officer.lua` | future Pope/Council authority module |
| `Roster` | `Core/Roster.lua` | live guild snapshot |
| `Gora` / `Ceremony` | matching `Core/*.lua` | domain records and ceremony flow — not scoring feeders |
| `Net` | `Net/BeefNet.lua` | send/recv, validate, dispatch into Core |
| `UI` | `UI/MainFrame.lua` (+ shell) | frames; views over Core |

## Coupling

```
✅ Roster update: GUILD_ROSTER_UPDATE → Roster:Refresh → UI refresh
✅ Net apply: BeefNet validate → Core store; UI reads copies

❌ Core → UI / CreateFrame / SendAddonMessage / slash
❌ UI recording official outcomes or inventing ranks
❌ Net inventing ranks or verdicts
❌ Second authority-gate outside Core/Officer.lua
❌ Guild promote/demote except the Pope verb KNIGHT THIS BEEF where the API permits (`pope-authority.mdc`)
```
